Polymorphing is optional, but can make your game a whole lot easier. There
are lots of things you can do, for example:

   1) Polypiling objects. This can be a useful intermediate step, after
      you've collected most of a kit from exploration but before burning
      wishes to fill in those stubborn missing bits.

   2) Poly your pet. There's often a polytrap in the mines, and it can
      be used to turn your dog or cat into something stupidly powerful.
      (And, you can keep trying until you like the result, though you
      risk getting a non-ambulatory pet, or one which cannot survive to
      the next attempt.)

   3) Controlled self-poly. If you have the resources at the right time,
      this can be a huge boost to early-game survivability. Later on, you
      can use it to manufacturer stoning grenades or to gobble rings and
      amulets. The unique abilities of the Xorn can be handy on some of
      the planes as well.

